# lo1re 0.1: the request-log sentence for ghostlights.theater/build-a-ghostwheel/, from register rows 0027 (access) 0028 (error) 0030 (note); sha256 30d7441f6daa8c355dde9bcef586bf0d218e4b78e7ca4abbe6c45a724b13538f
The web server at ghostlights.theater keeps a log of each request: the address that asked, the time, the page (without anything after a question mark), whether the page was found, and the browser's description of itself (kept to guess which requests are abuse). It keeps that log for up to 14 days, in a file of this site's own, to keep the site working and to guess which requests are abuse. When a request goes wrong, it also notes in an error log the address that asked, the time, the page, anything after a question mark in its address, how it asked (such as GET), the protocol version, the page that linked here (if your browser said), and the site's name; it keeps that for up to 14 days, in a file of this site's own, to keep the site working. Both are on the server, not in your browser, and forgetting here does not touch it.
